# Super_RCT Windows command table. Read by tools/gen_commands.py together with
# src/commands.def (regenerate with: python3 tools/gen_commands.py).
#
# Same format as commands.def. Only 'f' (file) and 'c' (program) entries here;
# built-ins are shared. Paths use drive letters. Program arguments are plain
# words (no shell): they are split on spaces and run directly, never through cmd.exe.
win_hosts|f|C:\Windows\System32\drivers\etc\hosts|Hosts file
win_networks|f|C:\Windows\System32\drivers\etc\networks|Network name file
win_win_ini|f|C:\Windows\win.ini|Windows settings file (win.ini)
win_ipconfig|c|ipconfig /all|IP configuration of all adapters
win_dns_cache|c|ipconfig /displaydns|DNS resolver cache
win_netstat|c|netstat -an|Listening and connected sockets
win_netstat_pid|c|netstat -ano|Sockets with owning process IDs
win_route|c|route print|Routing table
win_arp|c|arp -a|ARP cache
win_getmac|c|getmac /v /fo list|MAC addresses and transports
win_netsh_wlan|c|netsh wlan show interfaces|Wi-Fi interface status
win_firewall|c|netsh advfirewall show allprofiles|Firewall profile state
win_tasklist|c|tasklist|Running processes
win_tasklist_svc|c|tasklist /svc|Processes with their services
win_systeminfo|c|systeminfo|Full system information
win_driverquery|c|driverquery|Installed device drivers
win_pnp|c|pnputil /enum-devices /connected|Connected devices (PnP)
win_services|c|sc query type= service state= all|All Windows services and states
win_schtasks|c|schtasks /query /fo list|Scheduled tasks
win_time|c|w32tm /query /status|Windows time sync status
win_powercfg|c|powercfg /a|Sleep states supported
win_drives|c|fsutil fsinfo drives|Drive letters
win_volumes|c|mountvol|Mounted volumes
win_hostname|c|hostname|Computer name
